liuqin: stub the macOS-only names IOHIDDevice.cpp references

0270 vendored Apple's IOHIDDevice.cpp unchanged. It references four things that
do not exist on iOS (and are not in this tree):

  IOHIDSystemActivityTickle(kind, this)          x2, in updateActivityTickle
  IOHIKeyboard::message(kIOHIDSystemDeviceSeizeRequestMessage, ...)
  IOHIPointing::message(kIOHIDSystemDeviceSeizeRequestMessage, ...)
  NX_HARDWARE_TICKLE / NX_NULLEVENT              event kind constants

All of them sit on the seize/tickle path: a real keyboard or pointing device
being seized by IOHIDSystem. This port has no IOHIDSystem layer at all and the
digitizer never seizes anything, so the correct behaviour is to do nothing.
The header is included from IOHIDDevice.cpp behind ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_LIUQIN so
a future real port can drop it without touching Apple's source.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/LiuqinHIDMacOSStubs.h b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/LiuqinHIDMacOSStubs.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/LiuqinHIDMacOSStubs.h
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+/*
+ * LIUQIN: the macOS-only IOHIDDevice.cpp dependencies, as no-ops.
+ *
+ * IOHIDDevice.cpp is Apple source (IOHIDFamily-1915.140.3) kept unchanged.
+ * Four of the names it uses exist only in the macOS IOHIDSystem layer, which
+ * iOS does not have and this port certainly does not: this kernel has no
+ * IOHIDSystem, no IOHIKeyboard and no IOHIPointing. Every reference is on the
+ * seize/tickle path, which a digitizer never takes -- it seizes nothing and
+ * there is no system-wide tickle sink to poke.
+ *
+ * So: do nothing, quietly, and keep the call sites compiling.
+ */
+#ifndef LIUQIN_HID_MACOS_STUBS_H
+#define LIUQIN_HID_MACOS_STUBS_H
+
+/* NX event kinds IOHIDDevice.cpp passes to the tickle call. Values are the
+ * macOS ones (IOLLEvent.h) so a future port that grows a real tickle sink
+ * needs no change here; nothing on this port reads them. */
+#ifndef NX_NULLEVENT
+#define NX_NULLEVENT            0
+#endif
+#ifndef NX_HARDWARE_TICKLE
+#define NX_HARDWARE_TICKLE      24
+#endif
+
+/* kIOHIDSystemDeviceSeizeRequestMessage: the message IOHIDDevice sends to its
+ * provider when userland asks to seize the device. Unused on this port. */
+#ifndef kIOHIDSystemDeviceSeizeRequestMessage
+#define kIOHIDSystemDeviceSeizeRequestMessage 0xe0005000
+#endif
+
+/*
+ * IOHIDSystemActivityTickle: on macOS this wakes the event system so it
+ * re-evaluates idle time. There is no event system here; a tickle would only
+ * cost a lock on a service that does not exist.
+ */
+static inline void
+IOHIDSystemActivityTickle(int kind, IOService *sender)
+{
+	(void)kind;
+	(void)sender;
+}
+
+/*
+ * IOHIDDevice.cpp casts its provider to IOHIKeyboard / IOHIPointing and sends
+ * the seize message through them. Neither class exists on iOS, so the casts
+ * must yield NULL: declare the classes and give OSDynamicCast nothing to
+ * match. (OSDynamicCast needs a real OSObject subclass to compile.)
+ */
+class IOHIKeyboard : public IOService
+{
+	OSDeclareDefaultStructors(IOHIKeyboard)
+public:
+	using IOService::message;
+};
+
+class IOHIPointing : public IOService
+{
+	OSDeclareDefaultStructors(IOHIPointing)
+public:
+	using IOService::message;
+};
+
+#endif /* LIUQIN_HID_MACOS_STUBS_H */
